2026-08-07T14:05:02.2776642Z > # CRAN guard
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2776922Z > #
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2777594Z > # The duckdb test suite exercises DuckDB's bundled C++ engine, which is too heavy
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2778594Z > # for CRAN's check farm, and checks were very fragile in the past. We therefore
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2779530Z > # keep it off on CRAN but run it automatically on GitHub Actions (GITHUB_ACTIONS)
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2780499Z > # and on r-universe (MY_UNIVERSE). An explicit DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS opts in
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2781748Z > # (true-ish) or out (false-ish) and always wins; otherwise we fall back to those.
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2782764Z > # This check is intentionally inlined here (rather than calling into the package)
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2783682Z > # so the guard is obvious and self-contained.
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2784174Z > run_tests <- tolower(trimws(Sys.getenv("DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS", "")))
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2784495Z > 
2026-08-07T14:05:02.2784733Z > if (run_tests %in% c("true", "1", "yes", "on")) {
